# muse delivery sidecar via session-message + DeliveryEndpoint (CONDITIONAL-via-env)

## Status: PARKED per operator 2026-10-02 (Monitor-only posture)

Operator decision: stay Monitor-only for now — Monitor (while armed)
IS the push path (CONDITIONAL per repo taxonomy: external event pushes
into attention; GUARANTEED would need no operator arming). Revisit
this bug when either trigger fires: (a) a persistent (non-env)
session-ingress enable is found, or (b) the experimental flag
stabilizes / P1-P2 prove live-send wake and the gate is deemed
acceptable. The spec below is kept implementation-ready for that day.
B358 (managed) proceeds on hook + Monitor floor without this bug.

## Goal (when unparked)

Out-of-process push delivery for muse: drain broker inbox →
`muse session-message send --target` → drain-on-success. Honest wake
row: CONDITIONAL-via-env at best (experimental gate), promoted from
NONE only by the B352 P1/P2 verdicts (G1 wake + G3 B098-safe). If P1
or P2 refutes, this bug becomes "document NONE + keep Monitor floor"
instead of code — do not build on a refuted primitive.

## Contract

Transport (`C2c_muse_session_message`, new module, agy-agentapi
skeleton `ocaml/c2c_agy_agentapi.ml`):

- Pure `send_argv ~target ~body` (testable without the binary) +
  bounded `run_send` (15s TERM→KILL, agy L30–55 precedent).
- Target resolution: session name/uuid → live `message_capable`
  check via `session-message list` (registry goes stale — 5 JSONs
  vs 2 live sockets observed — so list, don't scan raw JSON);
  `launch_excluded` (exec sessions) addressed only if P1 proves
  delivery there, else fail closed with a clear message.
- Env gate: `MUSE_EXPERIMENTAL_EXTERNAL_AGENT_INGRESS=1` set by the
  sidecar/supervisor (documented as experimental); `classify_wake_env`
  (`Env_ready | Waiting_for_gate | Waiting_for_live_target`) à la
  agy :553; NO raw-env fallback that bypasses discovery (#78 lesson).
- B098-DATA-framed payload (`format_inbound_payload` precedent,
  agy :581): envelope + treat-as-data; NEVER user-role; never feed
  peer content to `turn/steer`-class APIs (MSP has `turn/steer` —
  same prohibition as Codex).

Sidecar loop (`c2c_muse_deliver.ml`, `c2c_agy_deliver.ml:111–221`
skeleton): ensure-env → PEEK inbox (+ global sessions-broker peek)
→ format envelopes → send → `drain_after_inject` with retry +
broker.log event; `_drain_owed` retry; race repair (drain's return
injected same cycle); `watched_pid`, `max_iterations`; persist-first
ordering is load-bearing (hermes `delivery.py:248–324`) — NEVER
drain-first; injector never drains.

Endpoint: `endpoint_of_muse_reg` + `module Muse : S` + `register`
in `ocaml/c2c_delivery_endpoint.ml` (`drain_policy=After_push`);
deliver-service watch-set + config keys
(`c2c_deliver_managed.ml:68–431` kimi/agy arms as template) behind a
`C2C_DELIVER_SERVICE_MUSE` gate; claim module only if dual-run is
possible (kimi-claim precedent).

Doctor: DEAF classifier (`classify_muse_session`: inbox>0 ∧ ¬poster
= DEAF, kimi pure precedent) + wake classifier
(`Muse_wake_none | Conditional_env_via_session_message`,
grok-monitor-lock precedent) + `--rearm` that skips confirmed-dead
(#42). Fixture gates `C2C_MUSE_*_FIXTURE` for every external effect.

## Acceptance

- Unit: argv purity, classify matrix, payload DATA-framing, endpoint
  probe/deliver/drain-policy, DEAF truth table.
- B098 regression mirroring `test_c2c_codex_autoturn_b098.ml`:
  verdict-shaped peer content delivered as DATA creates NO verdict
  file and satisfies NO approval.
- Hermetic sidecar tests (fixture `session-message`): peek→inject→
  drain success path, inject-failure leaves mail queued + owed-retry,
  race-repair path, gate-absent fail-closed message.
- Live proof (operator, scratch TUI): idle wake ×3 with latency +
  transcript placement + mid-turn behavior recorded; wake-guidance
  + doctor rows updated to match measured behavior exactly.

SCOPE (B352 verdicts, merged): RESCOPED — no out-of-process send primitive exists in muse 1.4.2 (CLI session-message containment-refused 9x; Tier-2 BLOCKED not CONDITIONAL). Ship as: (a) honest NONE-from-c2c-alone row + Monitor recipe (CONDITIONAL-via-Monitor), (b) session-message availability probe for doctor (gate? CLI refused? tool present?), (c) B098 regression from allow-body evidence (preview-only, Received-message placement). Revisit sending when a muse release admits an out-of-process sender. Park stands.